t  me and so i think everybody should be  them whoever that is whatever that is  so it's not a problem for me to you know  to be real because i just don't try to  put on any  false pretenses other than piling it on  on the  [Music]  my  outside  now of course dolly's music is  recognized across  generations but it was whitney houston's  famous rendition of i will always love  you  that catapulted her into the global  spotlight  whitney's 1992 take on the song for the  bodyguard soundtrack  recently surpassed one billion views on  youtube  and dolly recently opened up to et  canada's ros weston  about turning down elvis presley's  request to cover the ballad  i know you were very protective of that  song you were very protective of the  rights  you wanted to withhold them elvis wanted  to do it you had to turn them down  because they wanted  rights to the song all those years ago  when you made those decisions do you  sort of thank yourself every now and  then when you look around  and see your life and what that one song  has done for you  i would have loved to have heard elvis  sing the song it was not  elvis it was colonel tom who's his  manager that  you know said they had to have half  deposition but i still think about elvis  saying that  so i i have mixed i have mixed emotions  about that  but i am so grateful that it has done so  well  and like i say that's money i can put  into my family fund rather than  elvis family i was never so flattered  enough lord in my life and when whitney  did that and the incredible job that she  did and the  great success of the bodyguard movie  [Music]  you know and it being still considered  like one of  the greatest love songs ever i take  great pride in that i'm very humbled by  it  but she did an incredible job on that  now back in 2017 we sat down with the  grammy winner for the release of her  46th studio album and first children's  album i believe in you  where she opened up about that one  project she never got around to  having kids of her own my husband and i  were married 50 years  a couple years ago and we thought at the  start we would have children we even had  names for them now but it never did work  out that way  and then you know how time goes by and  you think well  i think it was not meant for us to have  kids so everybody's kids could be mine  because if we'd have had children  i probably wouldn't have spent as much  time and effort you know with other  people's children because you know how  it is if you got your own  you gotta you know take care of them and  save the money for them and make sure  they're  so i think it worked out really well  it's a well-known fact that dolly and  her husband of nearly  60 years carl dean keep their  relationship extremely private  and have done so since the beginning  this could definitely be the key to  keeping their romance strong  after so many years or maybe it's those  romantic date nights in their rv  camper that keeps the spark alive i mean  that sounds like a country love song  right there we don't do a lot of just  date nights our whole life is kind of  like a sweet thing but we'll  on anniversaries or on his birthday or  mine we'll go out to eat  and you know he doesn't like to get out  in public that much  but we we have our little rv camper we  go and i often cook in the mornings  like on weekends i'll cook and we pack  up a picnic basket and we'll go out to  the country and  find a riverbank we'll have picnics and  that sort of thing yeah  now somebody told me that you actually  enjoy uh going through like a taco bell  drive through together is that true well  yeah we go through all the  drive-throughs together  in our little rv it doesn't have to be  taco bell but we like that but we like  all of them  we hit them all and back in 2016 dolly  opened up about her secret wedding with  carl yeah for those who don't know  dolly actually met carl at a local  laundromat on the same day  she moved to nashville the pair quickly  got used to keeping their love for each  other  private because dolly's record label  thought a serious relationship would get  in the way  of her music career but no surprise  dolly proved them all wrong and managed  to make both  a success we had gone across the state  line in tennessee because  or into ringgold georgia because the  record label i was with asked me to not  get married because they had invested a  lot of money that was in 1966  they said wait here because we got money  tied up and our individual career we  went that same weekend sneaked off  across the state line and got married  and then of course a year later the  record label  everything was going good i was happy at  home but they said see  if you would have got married this  problem would have been going i said  i've been married for a year  and not having kids of their very own  gave dolly even more time to spend with  her goddaughter miley cyrus  over the years the pair have found  several opportunities to collaborate  together  including her very special appearances  on hannah montana of aunt  dolly  girls i don't just rock i roll  she's like one of my kids i've known her  since she's tiny little baby  and i've always known she was so  talented so gifted  and i knew what she was going through  when she was trying to make her own way  after hannah montana  and you know she i've said she's going  to always land on her feet no matter how  high she jumps  and you know it's like she and she has  and she will and more recently  of course dolly had to have miley on her  latest album a holly dolly christmas  where the two teamed up on the original  track christmas is  she had to sing on this christmas album  she was working on her own project i  said  i'm not going to ask you to put it out  of the single i know you got your own  thing  but you have to sing on this album with  me you and billy ray because you're like  family and i'm never  probably going to ever do another  christmas album i said